  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1201 AM CDT Fri Jun 19 2026\n\nA return to drier conditions for the weekend as zonal flow aloft\ndominates. Temperatures will be pretty close to normal for\nSaturday but a return to above normal readings by Sunday. Long\nrange models still continue to show an upper level ridge building\nover the southwest US for next week, placing the southern plains\ninto northwest flow. This favors afternoon/evening convection\nacross the Panhandle with the convection diving southeast towards\nthe Big County and Red River Valley overnight and into the morning\nhours. Thus, Big Country will see the highest POPs for the area\nfor Monday Night into Tuesday and then again TUesday Night into\nWednesday, with much more limited rain chances farther south and\nsouthwest. Temperatures will again be climbing well into the 90s\nand may be hitting the 100 degree mark across the northern and\nwestern Big Country.",
